[{:seon.task/name "a-reaction-is-tracked-by-the-stores-recorder"
  :seon.task/plan "The reaction core (docs/plan.md#the-root-concept-one-reaction-over-the-store, plan item 4), whole: web's half, taken over by context 2026-11-14 (root), built with seon.db's stored index (seon.reads-test/a-commits-datoms-rerun-the-readers-of-what-they-moved, jolt/context 205e329bb8) as one tip. The interface is Reagent's exactly, checked against its source (reagent-project/reagent fa4dc05, reference-code/reagent on jolt/deps: ratom.cljs track 238, track! 242, Track and cached-reaction 182-224, cursor 317; ratom.clj reaction 8, run! 15). What exists [M]: seon.ratom ports atom, Reaction, make-reaction, reaction, run!, flush!; the walk (seon.render) already runs each component in a reaction, records its store reads with datahike.api/with-reads as datom keys (:reads, the walk's :readers) and re-runs the readers of a commit's datom keys (queue-what-moved!); the render proc consumes the writer's :main notice ({:ops}). What duplicates it [M]: reads of the pulled tree are tracked a second way, by path (seon.ratom read-index, reached, prefixes and its sources/source-changed watch; the walk's :tree-readers; seon.ctx/changes as the change signal), and seon.render.proc keeps a third index (:read-index, reindex) over its views. Slice A: seon.ratom gains Reagent's track and track! (a Track, = on f and args, cached on the reaction in progress as cached-reaction does); the store is a source a reaction derefs: a deref records its datom keys through datahike.reads (one tracker) as the reaction's key set, and a commit's datoms re-run a reaction only when datahike.reads/reads-touched? holds on its key set. Slice B: a view's read of attribute a of a pulled entity e records [:ea e a], so the pulled tree's reads are datom keys and the path index goes; the render proc matches through the walk's one key set. Deletes: seon.ratom/read-index, reached, prefixes, the sources watch and source-changed; seon.render's :tree-readers and tree-reads; seon.render.proc's :read-index, reindex, index, unindex; seon.ctx/changes as a second change signal; the *reads* nil bypasses that exist only to dodge recording. Reaction, make-reaction and run! stay: they are the API. The stored :seon.reads/key-set's first production writer is a derived entity that outlives its process (tests' result, plan Stage 1.5); a walk's key sets stay in the walk value (root's ruling)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
